= BINSTD proposal prior-art source review

Observation, 2026-10-28. Four October 3 proposals account for four ledger metadata errors. This review read 20 hash-indexed repository records at main `fb55b843...`; it did not reread the underlying external papers or replay any run. All four cited BINSTD evidence records and the two decisions inspected here remain inconclusive. Proposal-to-evidence arrows pass through the named experiment specifications.

#image("lineage.svg", width: 100%)

`IDEA-43f871` and `IDEA-4f41d0` each put an internal `IDEA-*` pointer in `prior_art.nearest.ref`, where the schema accepts a known-result row or knowledge entry. The first has a valid adjacent trace card (`KR-IC-f5c584`); the second already has valid `KR-IC-5765d2` and `KR-IC-f5c584` entries, with the internal pointer named in a note. Preserve that lineage without calling the unpublished ideas literature.

`IDEA-94078e` and `IDEA-c9c6c3` have no `prior_art` block. Both cite `KR-IC-73db3f`, a heuristic factor-base vector-space card. A correction should be explicitly retrospective: the records do not prove a full prior-art search was performed when those proposals were created. The card does not prove the proposed catalog floors will hold.

Any correction needs hash-bound additive supersession and a complete-tree validator delta. No frozen record, performance graph, scientific verdict, or Lean proof is changed by this report. The absolute ledger gate remains red after the separate AUXIN correction (64 errors in 21 paths on its first hosted head).
